course: biology
lesson: 319
title: Bears by kind: the eight bears of the world
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: There are only eight kinds of bear in the whole world: the brown bear, the American black bear, the polar bear, the Asiatic black bear, the sun bear, the sloth bear, the spectacled bear and the giant panda.
explain: They share one body plan, big, strong and flat-footed with a short tail, but each has its own food and home, from sea ice to rainforest to bamboo mountains.
explain: Some names trick you. An American black bear can be brown or even white, the koala is not a bear at all, and the red panda is not a bear either.
explain: Think of the bears from stories: Baloo of The Jungle Book was a sloth bear, Paddington came from «darkest Peru» like the spectacled bear, and Po of Kung Fu Panda is a giant panda.
fact: The eight bears are the brown bear, American black bear, polar bear, Asiatic black bear, sun bear, sloth bear, spectacled bear and giant panda; the koala and the red panda are not bears.
fact: Brown bears live in North America, Europe and Asia; grizzlies and Kodiak bears are brown bears, a big Kodiak can weigh over 600 kilograms, and a hump of muscle on the shoulders helps them dig.
fact: In autumn brown bears gather at rivers to catch salmon swimming upstream, fattening up for winter.
fact: The polar bear is the most meat-eating bear, hunting seals on the sea ice and waiting at breathing holes because seals must come up for air; as the sea ice melts, polar bears must swim further and go hungry longer.
fact: American black bears can be black, brown, cinnamon or even white, like the spirit bear of Canada; it is the commonest bear in the world, with hundreds of thousands living wild, and it climbs trees easily.
fact: A study reported that white spirit bears catch more salmon by day than black ones, perhaps because a pale shape is harder for fish to see against the bright sky.
fact: The Asiatic black bear, or moon bear, has a cream-coloured crescent on its chest, lives in forests from Afghanistan to Japan, and bends branches into platforms in trees while feeding on nuts and fruit.
fact: The sun bear of Southeast Asia is the smallest bear, about as heavy as a big dog, with a very long tongue for licking honey and termites out of holes.
fact: In 2023 a sun bear in a Chinese zoo stood up so like a person that people online said it was a man in a costume, and the zoo said it was a real bear.
fact: The sloth bear of India and Sri Lanka has a gap where two upper front teeth are missing; it closes its nostrils, blows away dust and sucks termites up through the gap, and mothers carry their cubs on their backs.
fact: The spectacled bear of the Andes, with pale rings around its eyes, is the only bear in South America; it climbs trees and eats mostly plants and fruit.
fact: The giant panda is a true bear that eats almost only bamboo, but its gut is still a meat-eater's gut, so it digests little and must eat for many hours a day; since 2016 it has been listed as vulnerable instead of endangered.
fact: Wild bears that are half grizzly and half polar bear, called pizzly or grolar bears, have been found in the Canadian Arctic, as grizzlies wander further north into a warming Arctic.
exercise: How many kinds of bear are there in the world? | Eight | Two | Twenty | Eighty
exercise: Which of these is not a bear? | The koala | The sun bear | The sloth bear | The giant panda
exercise: Which bears are grizzlies and Kodiak bears? | Brown bears | Polar bears | Sun bears | Spectacled bears
exercise: What is a brown bear's shoulder hump? | Muscle that helps it dig | A store of water like a camel's | Fat for its cubs to drink | A broken bone that healed
exercise: Why do brown bears gather at rivers in autumn? | To catch salmon and fatten up for winter | To wash their thick fur clean before the winter sleep | To drink as much as they can | To meet the polar bears
exercise: Which is the most meat-eating bear? | The polar bear | The giant panda | The spectacled bear | The sun bear
exercise: Why does a polar bear wait by a hole in the ice? | Seals must come up there to breathe | It is fishing with its tongue | It is waiting for the ice to melt | It drinks from the hole
exercise: What colours can an American black bear be? | Black, brown, cinnamon or even white | Only ever black, which is how it got its name | Black and white like a panda | Only grey
exercise: Which is the commonest bear in the world? | The American black bear | The polar bear | The giant panda | The sun bear
exercise: What mark does an Asiatic black bear have on its chest? | A cream-coloured crescent like a V | Black and white stripes across the chest | A red spot | Pale rings like glasses
exercise: Which is the smallest bear? | The sun bear | The sloth bear | The spectacled bear | The polar bear
exercise: What does a sun bear use its very long tongue for? | Licking honey and termites out of holes | Catching fish in the sea | Cleaning its cubs only | Grabbing fruit from high trees
exercise: How does a sloth bear eat termites? | It blows away dust and sucks them up through a gap in its teeth | It waits with its mouth wide open until the termites crawl inside by themselves | It catches them in a web | It digs them up with its tail
exercise: How do sloth bear mothers carry their cubs? | On their backs | In a pouch | In their mouths all day | They never carry them
exercise: Where does the spectacled bear live? | In the Andes, the only bear in South America | In the hot, dry Australian bush, among the gum trees | In the Arctic | In Africa
exercise: Why must a giant panda eat bamboo for many hours a day? | Its gut is a meat-eater's gut and digests little of it | It must chew each leaf a hundred times before it is allowed to swallow | Bamboo is too delicious to stop | It gives the bamboo to its cubs
exercise: Why are grizzlies meeting polar bears more often? | Grizzlies wander further north as the Arctic warms | Polar bears are moving to forests in the south | People carry them to zoos together | They always lived side by side
test: Count them: a zoo keeps one bear of every kind in the world. How many bears is that? | 8 | 6 | 10 | 12
test: Count them: 3 sloth bear mothers each carry 2 cubs on their backs. How many bears in all? | 9 | 6 | 5 | 12
test: In Kung Fu Panda, Po gobbles dumplings and noodles all day. What does a real giant panda eat? | Almost only bamboo, for many hours a day | Mostly meat dumplings and bowls of noodles | Fish from rivers | Honey and berries only
test: In The Jungle Book Baloo is a lazy bear who loves ants. Which real bear was he, and what would it eat? | A sloth bear, sucking up termites and ants | A polar bear, eating seals on the sea ice | A panda, eating bamboo | A koala, eating leaves
test: Paddington Bear came from «darkest Peru». Which real bear lives there? | The spectacled bear of the Andes | The sun bear of the Peruvian jungle | The polar bear | The moon bear
test: «look that black bear is BROWN, someone named it wrong lol» What is right? | American black bears can be black, brown, cinnamon or even white | It must be a grizzly, black bears are only black | It is a black bear that got sunburnt | It is a panda without its spots
test: «ppl said the zoo sun bear was a guy in a bear suit lmao» What did the zoo say? | It was a real sun bear standing up like a person | It really was a man in a bear suit, there to fool the visitors | It was a statue | It was a robot made for visitors
test: What would happen to polar bears if there were much less sea ice for longer each year? | They would swim further and go hungry longer | They would hunt seals much more easily from the land | Nothing, they eat mainly grass | They would grow gills
test: «koalas are just little bears, my nan calls them koala bears» What is true? | Koalas are not bears at all, despite the name | Koalas are the smallest of the eight bears | Koalas are baby pandas | Koalas are bears that live only in trees
test: «saw a bear that's half white half brown in canada, a pizzly??» What could it be? | A wild hybrid of a grizzly and a polar bear, which has been found there | A polar bear that rolled in brown mud and could never wash it out again | Impossible, bears never mix | A panda painted by a joker
test: Why might a white spirit bear catch more fish by day than a black bear? | It is harder for fish to see against the bright sky | Fish like the colour white and swim up close to look at it | White bears swim faster | Black bears cannot swim at all
exam: Identify the number of extant species of bear. | Eight | Four | Twelve | Twenty-eight
exam: Select the response consistent with the established facts concerning the giant panda. | It is a true bear which subsists almost entirely upon bamboo, digesting it poorly | It is a member of the raccoon family which subsists principally upon meat and small birds | It is a marsupial which subsists upon eucalyptus | It is a true bear which subsists principally upon fish
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises the American black bear? | It is the most numerous bear and its coat may be black, brown, cinnamon or white | It is invariably black in colour and is confined to the Arctic coasts and the sea ice | It is the largest bear and dwells upon sea ice | It is a species of the Andes which is the sole bear in South America
exam: Ascertain the reason for which hybrids of the grizzly and the polar bear have been recorded in the Canadian Arctic. | Grizzlies have extended their range northward as the Arctic has warmed | Polar bears have migrated to southern forests in search of bamboo | Both species have been released together by zoological gardens | The two species have always shared identical habitats
